{"authored" [{"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A parcel robot begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(3i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}$ with an initial velocity of $(i-j)\\,\\text{cm/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "88e417ef5f2c6e5e6b3a14a39a47ebc257fe438e4bafb5fef985ce106681553d" "basis" 1622 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i+2j,\\,u=i-j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the parcel robot after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(18i+9j) \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(3i-3j)+(9i+4.5j) \\\\  & =(\\,15\\,i+3.5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "88e417ef5f2c6e5e6b3a14a39a47ebc257fe438e4bafb5fef985ce106681553d" "basis" 1622 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce" "basis" 1622 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "88e417ef5f2c6e5e6b3a14a39a47ebc257fe438e4bafb5fef985ce106681553d" "basis" 1622 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "88e417ef5f2c6e5e6b3a14a39a47ebc257fe438e4bafb5fef985ce106681553d" "basis" 1622 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-136420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(2i-4j)\\,{\\text{in/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(i-2j)\\,\\text{in/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=i-2j,\\,a=2i-4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(i-2j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i-4j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i-6j)+9(i-2j) \\\\  & =(3i-6j)+(9i-18j) \\\\  & =(12i-24j)\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38"} {"question" "q-136420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3i+14j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(-6i-7j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(12i+3j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(12i-24j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(8i+9j)\\,\\text{in}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(12i-24j)\\,\\text{in}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(4i+j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i+j,\\,a=-2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(4i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(16i+4j)+8(-2i+j) \\\\  & =(16i+4j)+(-16i+8j) \\\\  & =12j\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12j| \\\\  & =|12| \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{ft}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-136442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12\\,\\text{ft}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A parcel robot begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(3i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}$ with an initial velocity of $(i-j)\\,\\text{cm/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i+2j,\\,u=i-j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the parcel robot after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(18i+9j) \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(3i-3j)+(9i+4.5j) \\\\  & =(\\,15\\,i+3.5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A delivery drone starts from the point with position vector $(1i+2j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the drone to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An object moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the object to the origin$(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=-2i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the object after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+4j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-8i+16j) \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+(-4i+8j) \\\\  & =(2i+10j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the object to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{104} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{26}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{26}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "d3ce8dc90b62fafb5d965f1cc7fdd24b8d709407b2f8c5996085b9d9a5e294c6"}] "usage" {"q-280515" []} "basis" 1851 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186320852 17592186320853 17592186320855] "immutable_fields" [[17592186320851 :answer-field/correct] [17592186320851 :answer-field/id] [17592186320851 :answer-field/key] [17592186320851 :answer-field/type] [17592186320854 :answer-field/correct] [17592186320854 :answer-field/id] [17592186320854 :answer-field/key] [17592186320854 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
